    {
      "title": "Andhra SIPB clears projects worth ₹526 cr, to create about 9,000 jobs",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/andhra-sipb-clears-526-crore-projects-nearly-8-896-jobs-expected-126091800823_1.html",
      "description": "The Andhra Pradesh SIPB, headed by Chief Minister N Chandrababu Naidu, on Friday approved 10 projects entailing an investment of over Rs 500 crore.\nThe IT and futuristic technology projects are expected to create nearly 9,000 jobs, according to a press release.\n\"State Investment Promotion Board met today and officially cleared 10 major IT and futuristic technology projects. The approved projects entail a total investment of Rs 526.25 crore and are projected to create 8,896 high-quality jobs across the state,\" it said.\nThe approved projects include a Rs 100 crore investment by Muthoot Fincorp Limited to establish an Integrated Hub for AI and Tech Training Centre in Visakhapatnam.\nThe SIPB approved a Rs 44 crore investment by Deloitte to set up a state-of-the-art operations centre with a capacity of 2,500 seats.\nIt approved a Rs 167 crore investment by Quantum Codon Pvt Ltd in Amaravati to establish an integrated quantum AI-driven biotechnology innovation campus for drug discovery .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-18T12:57:24"
    }
